lisa-design:
- Added cache/throttle persistence as additive GORM model fields with `not null;default:0`, relying on the existing AutoMigrate path that already migrates dashboard suggestion run/cell models instead of adding a bespoke migration.
- Counted 429 pressure by best-effort incrementing the pending cell before returning `river.JobSnooze`; increment failures are logged only and do not alter snooze behavior.
- Sourced AI diagnostics queue stats directly from `river_job` for the `suggestion` queue instead of reusing notification troubleshooting because that service has a notification-only queue allow-list and job-kind filter.
- Returned `queue: null` plus a `queue_reachable` warning when `river_job` is unavailable or unreadable so diagnostics remain usable in test/dev databases without River tables.
- Used keyset pagination for `/admin/ai-diagnostics/runs` with an opaque base64 JSON cursor over `startedAt` and `id`; callers should treat the cursor as opaque.
- Kept AI diagnostics routes registered only inside the existing `config.AI.Enabled` gate and behind the admin middleware, so the endpoints are absent rather than returning disabled payloads when `CCF_AI_ENABLED=false`.

lisa-selfreview: pass 1 (verdict=request_changes)
- [medium] internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestion_diagnostics.go:364 (correctness): The diagnostics summary and run list read token/cache/rate-limit totals from dashboard_suggestion_runs, but those run-level rollups are only populated in finalizeRunIfReady after every cell has left pending. During an active run, completed cells already have input/cache tokens and snoozed pending cells already have rate_limited_count, yet /admin/ai-diagnostics/summary and /runs report zero for those values and rate_limit_pressure can pass while the run is actively being throttled.
- [low] internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestion_diagnostics.go:450 (correctness): The recent_failure_rate check claims to evaluate completed or failed cells from the last 24 hours, but loadRecentCellTotals filters by dashboard_suggestion_runs.started_at. A cell that completes or fails in the last 24 hours on a run started earlier is ignored, so the health check can miss recent failures from long-running or heavily snoozed runs.
